From d340e0dcbf4f94db544a2fd9820bc9de909cb9bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gopal Dhanve <gopaldhanve2003@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:46:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] keystore: Create keybox-attested keys through KeyMint

The keybox hook generated a throwaway software keypair inside the calling
app and cached a fake response for it. That path removed and re-added the
process-wide "BC" provider on every call; the framework copy has no EC
KeyPairGenerator, so key generation failed with "no such algorithm: EC for
provider BC" and apps that check key attestation got no valid chain.

Let KeyMint create the key and only rewrite its certificates:

 - KeyStoreSecurityLevel.generateKey asks KeyboxImitationHooks whether the
   keybox should attest the request. KeyMint generates the key with the
   original request first; if it cannot attest (broken or missing factory
   attestation keys), the request is retried with the attestation tags
   removed.
 - The certificate chain is then written to the real key with
   KeyStore2.updateSubcomponents: KeyMint's attested leaf is re-signed with
   the keybox, or a synthetic leaf is signed with the keybox when KeyMint
   returned none. Failing to prepare a chain fails key generation instead of
   returning an unattested certificate.
 - The getKeyEntry hook in KeyStore2 and the process-local response cache
   are removed.
 - KeyProviderManager gains isKeyboxAvailable(algorithm); loading and the
   spoof_keybox switch are unchanged. Certified props come from
   PropProviderManager.

Based on PixelOS changes 11608, 11713 and 11803 by Ashwin Devi Srinivasan,
adapted to the extra package and the Settings-driven providers.

